  "conclusion": "pyRho Fourier interpolation is exact for band-limited periodic fields and preserves the supplied sparse samples after phase alignment, but it cannot recover Fourier modes beyond the sparse-grid Nyquist limit. For this Si density, one shifted sparse request plus pyRho is a useful lossy approximation. Averaging all eight pyRho interpolants is still less accurate than direct interlacing and removes essentially all unrepresentable high-frequency power. Production CHGCAR reconstruction should therefore use direct interlacing when all residues are available; pyRho should be an explicitly lossy reduced-request mode followed by HALF/VASP validation."
